{"id": "cylab-py-cmdi-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-78", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.os-system", "before": "import os\n\ndef ping_host(host):\n    os.system(\"ping -c 1 \" + host)\n", "after": "import subprocess\n\ndef ping_host(host):\n    subprocess.run([\"ping\", \"-c\", \"1\", host], check=False)\n", "explanation_pt": "os.system com concatenação permite command injection (CWE-78). Prefira subprocess com lista de args, sem shell.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-py-path-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-22", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.path-join-user", "before": "from pathlib import Path\n\ndef read_user_file(name):\n    path = Path(\"/var/data\") / name\n    return path.read_text()\n", "after": "from pathlib import Path\n\ndef read_user_file(name):\n    base = Path(\"/var/data\").resolve()\n    path = (base / name).resolve()\n    if not str(path).startswith(str(base)):\n        raise ValueError(\"path traversal\")\n    return path.read_text()\n", "explanation_pt": "Nome de arquivo controlado pelo usuário pode escapar o diretório base (CWE-22). Normalize e confira o prefixo.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-py-pickle-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-502", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.pickle-loads", "before": "import pickle\n\ndef load_session(blob):\n    return pickle.loads(blob)\n", "after": "import json\n\ndef load_session(blob):\n    return json.loads(blob)\n", "explanation_pt": "pickle.loads em dados não confiáveis permite RCE (CWE-502). Use formato seguro (JSON) ou assinatura + allowlist.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-py-ssrf-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-918", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.requests-url-user", "before": "import requests\n\ndef fetch(url):\n    return requests.get(url).text\n", "after": "import requests\nfrom urllib.parse import urlparse\n\nALLOWED = {\"api.example.com\"}\n\ndef fetch(url):\n    host = urlparse(url).hostname\n    if host not in ALLOWED:\n        raise ValueError(\"host not allowed\")\n    return requests.get(url, timeout=5).text\n", "explanation_pt": "URL controlada pelo usuário sem allowlist causa SSRF (CWE-918). Valide esquema/host e use timeout.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-py-crypto-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-328", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.md5-password", "before": "import hashlib\n\ndef hash_password(pw):\n    return hashlib.md5(pw.encode()).hexdigest()\n", "after": "import hashlib\nimport secrets\n\ndef hash_password(pw):\n    salt = secrets.token_bytes(16)\n    dk = hashlib.pbkdf2_hmac(\"sha256\", pw.encode(), salt, 200_000)\n    return salt.hex() + \":\" + dk.hex()\n", "explanation_pt": "MD5 não é adequado para senha (CWE-328). Use KDF com salt (PBKDF2/Argon2/bcrypt).", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-py-xss-tpl-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-79", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.flask-unsafe-html", "before": "from flask import Flask, request, Markup\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\ndef index():\n    name = request.args.get(\"name\", \"\")\n    return Markup(f\"<h1>Olá {name}</h1>\")\n", "after": "from flask import Flask, request, escape\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.get(\"/\")\ndef index():\n    name = request.args.get(\"name\", \"\")\n    return f\"<h1>Olá {escape(name)}</h1>\"\n", "explanation_pt": "HTML com entrada crua causa XSS (CWE-79). Escape a saída ou use template com autoescape.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-js-sqli-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-89", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.sql-concat", "before": "async function getUser(db, id) {\n  const q = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = \" + id;\n  return db.query(q);\n}\n", "after": "async function getUser(db, id) {\n  const q = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?\";\n  return db.query(q, [id]);\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "Concatenar id na query SQL permite injeção (CWE-89). Use query parametrizada.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-js-cmdi-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-78", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.child-exec", "before": "const { exec } = require(\"child_process\");\n\nfunction listDir(userPath) {\n  exec(\"ls \" + userPath, (err, out) => console.log(out));\n}\n", "after": "const { execFile } = require(\"child_process\");\n\nfunction listDir(userPath) {\n  execFile(\"ls\", [\"-la\", \"--\", userPath], (err, out) => console.log(out));\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "exec com string montada permite command injection (CWE-78). Use execFile com args separados.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-js-path-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-22", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.path-join-user", "before": "const fs = require(\"fs\");\nconst path = require(\"path\");\n\nfunction readUpload(name) {\n  return fs.readFileSync(path.join(\"/uploads\", name), \"utf8\");\n}\n", "after": "const fs = require(\"fs\");\nconst path = require(\"path\");\n\nfunction readUpload(name) {\n  const base = path.resolve(\"/uploads\");\n  const full = path.resolve(base, name);\n  if (!full.startsWith(base + path.sep)) throw new Error(\"path traversal\");\n  return fs.readFileSync(full, \"utf8\");\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "path.join com nome do usuário permite path traversal (CWE-22). Resolve e valide o prefixo.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-js-xss-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-79", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.innerhtml-user", "before": "function greet(el, name) {\n  el.innerHTML = \"<p>Olá \" + name + \"</p>\";\n}\n", "after": "function greet(el, name) {\n  el.textContent = \"\";\n  const p = document.createElement(\"p\");\n  p.textContent = \"Olá \" + name;\n  el.appendChild(p);\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "innerHTML com dados do usuário causa XSS (CWE-79). Use textContent/DOM APIs.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-js-eval-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-95", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.eval-user", "before": "function runMath(expr) {\n  return eval(expr);\n}\n", "after": "function runMath(expr) {\n  if (!/^[0-9+\\-*/().\\s]+$/.test(expr)) throw new Error(\"invalid\");\n  return Function('\"use strict\"; return (' + expr + ')')();\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "eval em entrada arbitrária é code injection (CWE-95). Restrinja a expressão ou use parser seguro.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-js-proto-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-1321", "source": "cylab-synthetic", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.merge-proto", "before": "function merge(a, b) {\n  for (const k of Object.keys(b)) a[k] = b[k];\n  return a;\n}\n", "after": "function merge(a, b) {\n  for (const k of Object.keys(b)) {\n    if (k === \"__proto__\" || k === \"constructor\" || k === \"prototype\") continue;\n    a[k] = b[k];\n  }\n  return a;\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "Merge raso sem filtrar chaves especiais permite prototype pollution (CWE-1321).", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-sqli-002", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-89", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.sql-injection", "before": "import sqlite3\n\ndef by_name(conn, name):\n    cur = conn.cursor()\n    cur.execute(f\"SELECT id FROM people WHERE name = '{name}'\")\n    return cur.fetchall()\n", "after": "import sqlite3\n\ndef by_name(conn, name):\n    cur = conn.cursor()\n    cur.execute(\"SELECT id FROM people WHERE name = ?\", (name,))\n    return cur.fetchall()\n", "explanation_pt": "f-string no execute permite SQL injection (CWE-89). Use placeholder e tupla de parâmetros.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-secret-002", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-798", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.hardcoded-secret", "before": "aws_secret = \"wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY\"\n\ndef creds():\n    return {\"secret\": aws_secret}\n", "after": "import os\n\ndef creds():\n    return {\"secret\": os.environ[\"AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY\"]}\n", "explanation_pt": "Segredo AWS no código (CWE-798). Use variável de ambiente ou IAM role.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-secret-002", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-798", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.hardcoded-secret", "before": "const apiToken = \"ghp_exampleHardcodedToken000000\";\n\nfunction headers() {\n  return { Authorization: \"Bearer \" + apiToken };\n}\n", "after": "function headers() {\n  const apiToken = process.env.API_TOKEN;\n  if (!apiToken) throw new Error(\"API_TOKEN missing\");\n  return { Authorization: \"Bearer \" + apiToken };\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "Token hardcoded (CWE-798). Leia de process.env.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-xxe-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-611", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.xml-xxe", "before": "from lxml import etree\n\ndef parse_upload(path):\n    return etree.parse(path)\n", "after": "from lxml import etree\n\ndef parse_upload(path):\n    parser = etree.XMLParser(resolve_entities=False, no_network=True)\n    return etree.parse(path, parser)\n", "explanation_pt": "Parser XML padrão pode resolver entidades externas (XXE, CWE-611). Desative entidades e rede.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-debug-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-489", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.flask-debug", "before": "from flask import Flask\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app.run(host=\"0.0.0.0\", debug=True)\n", "after": "from flask import Flask\nimport os\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app.run(host=\"0.0.0.0\", debug=os.getenv(\"FLASK_DEBUG\") == \"1\")\n", "explanation_pt": "debug=True expõe interactive debugger (CWE-489). Só ative via config explícita de ambiente.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-assert-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-617", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.assert-auth", "before": "def delete_all(user):\n    assert user.is_admin\n    return wipe_db()\n", "after": "def delete_all(user):\n    if not user.is_admin:\n        raise PermissionError(\"admin only\")\n    return wipe_db()\n", "explanation_pt": "assert some com -O e não é controle de acesso (CWE-617). Use if + exceção.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-cmdi-shell-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-78", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.command-injection", "before": "import subprocess\n\ndef convert(path):\n    subprocess.call(\"convert \" + path + \" out.png\", shell=True)\n", "after": "import subprocess\n\ndef convert(path):\n    subprocess.run([\"convert\", path, \"out.png\"], check=False)\n", "explanation_pt": "shell=True com path externo = command injection (CWE-78). Lista de args sem shell.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-sqli-tpl-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-89", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.sql-injection", "before": "async function find(db, city) {\n  return db.query(`SELECT * FROM stores WHERE city = '${city}'`);\n}\n", "after": "async function find(db, city) {\n  return db.query(\"SELECT * FROM stores WHERE city = ?\", [city]);\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "Template string no SQL permite injeção (CWE-89). Parametrize.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-cors-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-942", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.cors-star", "before": "function setCors(res) {\n  res.setHeader(\"Access-Control-Allow-Origin\", \"*\");\n}\n", "after": "const ALLOWED = new Set([\"https://app.example.com\"]);\n\nfunction setCors(res, origin) {\n  if (ALLOWED.has(origin)) res.setHeader(\"Access-Control-Allow-Origin\", origin);\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "CORS * com credenciais/APIs sensíveis é perigoso (CWE-942). Allowlist de origens.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-weakhash-001", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-328", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.weak-hash", "before": "const crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n\nfunction fingerprint(pw) {\n  return crypto.createHash(\"md5\").update(pw).digest(\"hex\");\n}\n", "after": "const crypto = require(\"crypto\");\n\nfunction fingerprint(pw) {\n  const salt = crypto.randomBytes(16);\n  const hash = crypto.scryptSync(pw, salt, 32);\n  return salt.toString(\"hex\") + \":\" + hash.toString(\"hex\");\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "MD5 não serve para senha (CWE-328). Use scrypt/bcrypt/argon2 com salt.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-ts-random-001", "lang": "typescript", "cwe": "CWE-338", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.typescript.insecure-randomness", "before": "export function resetToken(): string {\n  return Math.random().toString(36).slice(2);\n}\n", "after": "import { randomBytes } from \"crypto\";\n\nexport function resetToken(): string {\n  return randomBytes(32).toString(\"hex\");\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "Math.random não é CSPRNG (CWE-338). Use crypto.randomBytes.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-deser-001", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-502", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.insecure-deserialization", "before": "import yaml\n\ndef load_cfg(raw):\n    return yaml.load(raw)\n", "after": "import yaml\n\ndef load_cfg(raw):\n    return yaml.safe_load(raw)\n", "explanation_pt": "yaml.load inseguro deserializa objetos arbitrários (CWE-502). Use safe_load.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-cmdi-002", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-78", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.command-injection", "before": "const { exec } = require(\"child_process\");\n\nexports.zip = (req, res) => {\n  exec(\"zip -r out.zip \" + req.body.dir, (e, out) => res.send(out));\n};\n", "after": "const { execFile } = require(\"child_process\");\n\nexports.zip = (req, res) => {\n  execFile(\"zip\", [\"-r\", \"out.zip\", \"--\", req.body.dir], (e, out) => res.send(out));\n};\n", "explanation_pt": "exec com body.dir = command injection (CWE-78). execFile + args.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-sqli-003", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-89", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.sql-injection", "before": "def lookup(cur, uid):\n    cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM t WHERE id = %s\" % uid)\n", "after": "def lookup(cur, uid):\n    cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM t WHERE id = %s\", (uid,))\n", "explanation_pt": "Formatação % no SQL é injeção (CWE-89). Passe o valor como parâmetro bindado.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-sqli-004", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-89", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.sql-injection", "before": "def lookup(cur, uid):\n    cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM t WHERE id = {}\".format(uid))\n", "after": "def lookup(cur, uid):\n    cur.execute(\"SELECT * FROM t WHERE id = ?\", (uid,))\n", "explanation_pt": ".format no SQL é injeção (CWE-89). Use placeholder.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-cmdi-002", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-78", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.command-injection", "before": "import os\n\ndef run(cmd):\n    os.system(cmd)\n", "after": "import subprocess\n\ndef run(args):\n    subprocess.run(args, check=False)\n", "explanation_pt": "os.system com string arbitrária (CWE-78). Use subprocess com lista.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-secret-003", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-798", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.hardcoded-secret", "before": "password = \"admin123456\"\n\ndef db_url():\n    return \"postgres://user:\" + password + \"@localhost/db\"\n", "after": "import os\n\ndef db_url():\n    password = os.environ[\"DB_PASSWORD\"]\n    return \"postgres://user:\" + password + \"@localhost/db\"\n", "explanation_pt": "Senha no código (CWE-798). Use env.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-hash-002", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-328", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.weak-hash", "before": "import hashlib\n\ndef token(data):\n    return hashlib.sha1(data.encode()).hexdigest()\n", "after": "import hashlib\nimport hmac\nimport os\n\ndef token(data):\n    key = os.environb[\"APP_HMAC_KEY\"]\n    return hmac.new(key, data.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n", "explanation_pt": "SHA1 fraco para token/integridade sensível (CWE-328). Prefira HMAC-SHA256 com chave.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-xss-002", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-79", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.xss-innerhtml", "before": "function render(el, msg) {\n  el.innerHTML = msg;\n}\n", "after": "function render(el, msg) {\n  el.textContent = msg;\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "innerHTML com msg externa = XSS (CWE-79). textContent.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-secret-003", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-798", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.hardcoded-secret", "before": "const secretKey = \"local-dev-secret-do-not-use\";\nmodule.exports = { secretKey };\n", "after": "const secretKey = process.env.SECRET_KEY;\nif (!secretKey) throw new Error(\"SECRET_KEY required\");\nmodule.exports = { secretKey };\n", "explanation_pt": "secretKey literal (CWE-798). Env obrigatória.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-sql-002", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-89", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.sql-injection", "before": "function del(db, id) {\n  return db.query(\"DELETE FROM items WHERE id = \" + id);\n}\n", "after": "function del(db, id) {\n  return db.query(\"DELETE FROM items WHERE id = ?\", [id]);\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "DELETE com concat = SQLi (CWE-89).", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-ts-rand-002", "lang": "typescript", "cwe": "CWE-338", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.typescript.insecure-randomness", "before": "export function otp(): string {\n  return String(Math.floor(Math.random() * 1_000_000)).padStart(6, \"0\");\n}\n", "after": "import { randomInt } from \"crypto\";\nexport function otp(): string {\n  return String(randomInt(0, 1_000_000)).padStart(6, \"0\");\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "OTP com Math.random (CWE-338). Use crypto.randomInt.", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-flask-xss-002", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-79", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.flask-unsafe-html", "before": "from flask import Markup, request\n\ndef page():\n    return Markup(\"<b>\" + request.args[\"q\"] + \"</b>\")\n", "after": "from flask import escape, request\n\ndef page():\n    return \"<b>\" + escape(request.args[\"q\"]) + \"</b>\"\n", "explanation_pt": "Markup com query string = XSS (CWE-79). escape().", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-js-proto-002", "lang": "javascript", "cwe": "CWE-1321", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.javascript.merge-proto", "before": "function assign(target, src) {\n  for (const k of Object.keys(src)) target[k] = src[k];\n  return target;\n}\n", "after": "function assign(target, src) {\n  for (const k of Object.keys(src)) {\n    if (k === \"__proto__\" || k === \"constructor\") continue;\n    target[k] = src[k];\n  }\n  return target;\n}\n", "explanation_pt": "Merge sem filtro = prototype pollution (CWE-1321).", "split": "train"}
{"id": "cylab-sam-py-sqli-005", "lang": "python", "cwe": "CWE-89", "source": "sintetico-cylab", "license": "CC-BY-4.0", "opengrep_rule": "cylab.python.sql-injection", "before": "def q(cur, x):\n    cur.execute(f\"UPDATE t SET a=1 WHERE id={x}\")\n", "after": "def q(cur, x):\n    cur.execute(\"UPDATE t SET a=1 WHERE id=?\", (x,))\n", "explanation_pt": "UPDATE com f-string = SQLi (CWE-89).", "split": "train"}
